# Comments

Write as if a first-time reader opened this file (code, docs, skills, rules). Add a comment only when it provides context that cannot be reasonably inferred from the surrounding text.

## NEVER

* Comments that exist because you just changed something ("no longer X", "we used to Y", "do not do Z — we removed Z")
* Restating what the next line does
* Documenting the absence of a deleted feature or an alternative you did not take

## ALWAYS

* Comment only standing invariants a first-time reader would otherwise miss: non-obvious constraints or why the obvious approach is wrong.
